	"metadata": {
		"pactSpecification": {
			"version": "3.0.0"
		},
		"provenance": "Consumer expectations (plan 0024, HoBo.CD GitHub Pages realizer) against the GitHub REST API (X-GitHub-Api-Version 2022-11-28): repository read, Pages site read/delete, Pages builds, the Git Data API (blobs, trees, commits, refs), Actions artifacts, Pages deployments (by build version) and github-pages environment deployments and statuses, as documented at docs.github.com/rest. Recorded from the offline world in test/support/world.ts by HOBO_PACT_RECORD=1; not provider-verified or captured live traffic. Response headers follow GitHub's documented set (x-github-request-id, x-github-media-type, x-ratelimit-limit/remaining/used/reset/resource, x-accepted-github-permissions on a permission 403, retry-after on a secondary rate limit) and error bodies GitHub's {message, documentation_url, status}; request ids and rate-limit counters are fixture values. Git object ids are real: blob and tree ids are what git computes for the fixture site.",
		"matching": "Requests match on method, templated path ({sha}, {deployment_id}, {artifact_id}), query, the top-level request-body key set and the response status, plus the rate-limit variant of a 403 (x-ratelimit-remaining 0 is a primary limit, retry-after a secondary one); response status, headers and bodies are served verbatim by the offline world, and every refusal interaction is replayed into the resolver. File bytes and the OIDC token are placeholders."
	},
